      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hit this in a clean build environment. Syncconfig fails because `scripts/as-version.sh` calls `scripts/min-tool-version.sh`, but that helper is not present in this 4.19 tree:\n\n`../scripts/as-version.sh: 59: ../scripts/min-tool-version.sh: not found`\n`scripts/Kconfig.include:56: Sorry, this assembler is not supported.`\n\nSo the issue is not the assembler version itself, but the missing helper used by\nthe minimum version check.\n\nNathan\u0027s 5.10 backport also drops the minimum version checking part, which is\nthe reasoning I followed here:\nhttps://github.com/aosp-mirror/kernel_common/commit/83f55e6f298e9e79a38b92d771179090ff0ac771",
